{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-4789-a0b1-c2d3e4f56789",
		"name": "TCSS-460 Message API - Comprehensive Test Suite",
		"description": "Complete Postman collection for testing all endpoints of the TCSS-460 Message API, including public routes, protected routes, authentication, and documentation endpoints.\n\nGenerated from: swagger.yaml\nBase URL: http://localhost:8000\n\n## Collection Structure\n\n1. **Health Check** - Server health monitoring\n2. **Authentication** - API key generation and form\n3. **Public Messages** - CRUD operations without authentication\n4. **Protected Messages** - CRUD operations requiring API key\n5. **Documentation** - Educational documentation endpoints\n\n## Variables\n\n- `baseUrl`: http://localhost:8000\n- `apiKey`: Set automatically after generating API key in Authentication folder\n- `testName`: Dynamic name for test messages\n- `testMessage`: Sample message content\n\n## Testing Workflow\n\n1. Run \"Health Check\" to verify server is running\n2. Generate API key using \"POST Generate API Key\" (saves key to collection variable)\n3. Test public message endpoints (no authentication required)\n4. Test protected message endpoints (uses saved API key)\n5. Explore documentation endpoints\n\n## Educational Focus\n\nThis collection demonstrates:\n- RESTful API design patterns\n- Stateful authentication with API keys\n- Request validation and error handling\n- CRUD operations with PostgreSQL\n- HTTP method semantics (GET, POST, PATCH, DELETE)",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
	"item": [
		{
			"name": "1. Health Check",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "GET Health Check",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 200\", function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(200);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test(\"Response has status and timestamp\", function () {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('status');",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData).to.have.property('timestamp');",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.status).to.eql('OK');",
									"});"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/health",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"health"
							]
						},
						"description": "Returns the current health status of the API server with timestamp.\n\n**Expected Response:**\n```json\n{\n  \"status\": \"OK\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2024-01-15T10:30:00.000Z\"\n}\n```"
					},
					"response": []
				}
			],
			"description": "System health and status monitoring endpoints"
		},
		{
			"name": "2. Authentication",
			"item": [
				{
					"name": "GET API Key Form (HTML)",
					"request": {
						"method": "GET",
						"header": [],
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api-key",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api-key"
							]
						},
						"description": "Returns an HTML page with a form to generate a new API key.\n\n**Response Type:** text/html\n\nThis endpoint demonstrates how APIs can serve both JSON and HTML content."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
					"name": "POST Generate API Key",
					"event": [
						{
							"listen": "test",
							"script": {
								"exec": [
									"pm.test(\"Status code is 201\", function () {",
									"    pm.response.to.have.status(201);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test(\"Response contains API key\", function () {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.success).to.be.true;",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('api_key');",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('name');",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('created_at');",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.data).to.have.property('usage');",
									"    ",
									"    // Save API key to collection variable for use in protected endpoints",
									"    pm.collectionVariables.set('apiKey', jsonData.data.api_key);",
									"    console.log('API Key saved to collection variable:', jsonData.data.api_key);",
									"});",
									"",
									"pm.test(\"API key is valid UUID v4 format\", function () {",
									"    var jsonData = pm.response.json();",
									"    var uuidV4Pattern = /^[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-4[0-9a-f]{3}-[89ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$/i;",
									"    pm.expect(jsonData.data.api_key).to.match(uuidV4Pattern);",
									"});"
								],
								"type": "text/javascript"
							}
						}
					],
					"request": {
						"method": "POST",
						"header": [
							{
								"key": "Content-Type",
								"value": "application/json"
							}
						],
						"body": {
							"mode": "raw",
							"raw": "{\n  \"name\": \"{{$randomFullName}}\",\n  \"email\": \"{{$randomEmail}}\"\n}"
						},
						"url": {
							"raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api-key",
							"host": [
								"{{baseUrl}}"
							],
							"path": [
								"api-key"
							]
						},
						"description": "Generates a new API key for authentication with protected endpoints.\n\n**Process:**\n1. Validates name and email\n2. Generates a cryptographically secure UUID v4 key\n3. Stores key in database with metadata\n4. Returns key (shown only once - must be saved!)\n\n**Request Body:**\n- `name` (required): 1-255 characters\n- `email` (required): valid email format\n\n**Note:** The generated API key is automatically saved to the collection variable `apiKey` for use in protected endpoint requests."
					},
					"response": []
				},
				{
